{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"92548a26-da6e-4683-9bdf-96deb479e1fa","agentId":"a3bf9b52fb2ec01e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes. Token-efficient; report under 100 words. Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; file to extend: mes-log-mcp/mes/experience.py (LINKS entries; see its schema and docstring) and its test mes-log-mcp/tests/check_experience.py. Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe.\n\nThe Alfa forums (stelvioforum.com, giuliaforums.com, alfabb.com, alfaowner.com) return HTTP 202 (a JS bot wall) to plain HTTP clients, so no forum threads were added. Verify them the way a browser does instead: drive headless Edge over the DevTools Protocol (copy the minimal CDP pattern from cuore/tests/check_live_widgets.py; kill Edge afterwards with cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py), navigate to each URL in C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\forum_urls.txt (candidate thread URLs found earlier), wait up to 8 s, and read document.title + the first post's text (first 300 chars). A URL is verified if the title is a real thread title (not \"Just a moment\", \"Attention Required\", or an error) and the page contains post text. For each verified thread add a LINKS entry: source = the forum, kind = \"forum_thread\", title = the page title, covers = one sentence from the first post, keys from the thread's topic (EVAP/P0455/P0456/P0440, esim, purge_valve, canister, window_riser, network_cascade, battery_12v, transfer_case, oil_change, etc.), reputation \"high\" for threads with many replies, verified_how = \"browser_cdp\", verified_at = \"2026-10-07\". If forum_urls.txt has fewer than 10 usable URLs, do up to 2 quick web searches for Stelvio/Giulia EVAP P0455/P0456 ESIM threads and window-riser B1176 threads on those forums and verify those too. Drop anything unverified. Update the test to require at least one forum_thread for P0455 if you verified one. Run check_experience.py and check_server.py."},"uuid":"c3b41da6-6e47-4b50-a6eb-6a918264bb3b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:39:11.670Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
