       \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n   328\t        \"covers\": \"12V main battery replacement on a Stelvio, framed around chasing \"\n   329\t                  \"electrical gremlins back to a weak battery.\",\n   330\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"stelvio_2.0t\",\n   331\t        \"date\": None,\n   332\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n   333\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n   334\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n   335\t    },\n   336\t    {\n   337\t        \"id\": \"yt-12v-battery-giulia\",\n   338\t        \"keys\": [\"battery_12v\"],\n   339\t        \"title\": \"🍀 Alfa Romeo Giulia Battery Replacement 🍀\",\n   340\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RvVCRASmRc8\",\n   341\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n   342\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n   343\t        \"covers\": \"12V battery swap on a Giulia, same procedure/location as the Stelvio.\",\n   344\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"giulia_2.0t\",\n   345\t        \"date\": None,\n   346\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n   347\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n   348\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n   349\t    },\n   350\t\n   351\t    # --- tpms ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   352\t    {\n   353\t        \"id\": \"yt-tpms-reset-giulia\",\n   354\t        \"keys\": [\"tpms\"],\n   355\t        \"title\": \"How to Reset Tire Pressure on an Alfa Romeo Giulia\",\n   356\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/aZozbSTK_ec\",\n   357\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n   358\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n   359\t        \"covers\": \"In-cluster/infotainment menu walk to reset the TPMS pressure warning \"\n   360\t                  \"on a Giulia; same menu path as the Stelvio.\",\n   361\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"giulia_2.0t\",\n   362\t        \"date\": None,\n   363\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n   364\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n   365\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n   366\t    },\n   367\t\n   368\t    # --- zf8hp_fluid -----------------------------------------------------\n   369\t    {\n   370\t        \"id\": \"yt-zf8hp-transmission-service\",\n   371\t        \"keys\": [\"zf8hp_fluid\"],\n   372\t        \"title\": \"Alfa Romeo Gulia/Stelvio transmission service\",\n   373\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PcCrAYIjLTU\",\n   374\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n   375\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n   376\t        \"covers\": \"ZF 8HP fluid/filter service on the shared Giulia/Stelvio AWD drivetrain.\",\n   377\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"giorgio\",\n   378\t        \"date\": None,\n   379\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n   380\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n   381\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n   382\t    },\n   383\t)\n   384\t\n   385\t\n   386\tdef _norm(key: str) -> str:\n   387\t    return (key or \"\").strip()\n   388\t\n   389\t\n   390\tdef for_code(code: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n   391\t    \"\"\"All entries tagged with this exact DTC (e.g. ``\"P0455\"``).\"\"\"\n   392\t    key = _norm(code).upper()\n   393\t    return [e for e in LINKS if key in e[\"keys\"]]\n   394\t\n   395\t\n   396\tdef for_family(family: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n   397\t    \"\"\"All entries tagged with this fault family (e.g. ``\"EVAP\"``).\"\"\"\n   398\t    key = _norm(family)\n   399\t    return [e for e in LINKS if key in e[\"keys\"]]\n   400\t\n   401\t\n   402\tdef for_job(job: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n   403\t    \"\"\"All entries tagged with this service job (e.g. ``\"oil_change\"``).\"\"\"\n   404\t    key = _norm(job)\n   405\t    return [e for e in LINKS if key in e[\"keys\"]]\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\tdef all() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n   409\t    \"\"\"Every tabulated entry, unfiltered.\"\"\"\n   410\t    return list(LINKS)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b97db386-10df-4e20-a0d3-10b4632f5ec9","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:40:42.556Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"     1\t\"\"\"Others' experience: reputable YouTube how-tos and direct forum threads.\n     2\t\n     3\tA mechanic's dossier is codes, specs and bulletins; what it is missing is the\n     4\tthing a shop floor actually runs on -- \"I've seen this exact code on this\n     5\texact car, here's what it was.\" This module is a small, hand-curated,\n     6\tlink-verified table pointing at that: specific YouTube videos showing the\n     7\tactual Alfa Romeo/Stellantis Giorgio-platform part being worked on, and (where\n     8\tverification allowed it -- see below) direct forum threads, keyed by DTC,\n     9\tfault family or service job.\n    10\t\n    11\tEvery entry was checked on 2026-10-07 (``verified_at``) either by an HTTP GET\n    12\treturning 200 with a browser User-Agent (``verified_how: \"http_200\"``) or via\n    13\tthe YouTube oEmbed endpoint returning 200 with a title (``verified_how:\n    14\t\"youtube_oembed\"``, and that returned title is stored verbatim). Nothing\n    15\tbelow was invented and nothing that failed verification was kept.\n    16\t\n    17\tKNOWN LIMITATION -- forum threads: stelvioforum.com, giuliaforums.com,\n    18\talfabb.com and alfaowner.com (all XenForo, apparently sharing one vendor) sit\n    19\tbehind a JavaScript proof-of-work bot challenge that returns HTTP 202 with a\n    20\tchallenge page to any plain HTTP client, never the real thread -- confirmed\n    21\tagainst a dozen thread URLs across all four domains during this build. A\n    22\tplain ``urllib``/``requests`` GET cannot pass that challenge (it requires\n    23\texecuting the page's JS), so no thread on those four domains could be\n    24\tverified as HTTP 200 and none is included here, even though the threads\n    25\tthemselves clearly exist and are on-topic. The practical effect: this table\n    26\tis YouTube-heavy and forum-light. If a future verification pass gains a way\n    27\tto pass that challenge (a real browser session, a cookie jar primed by one),\n    28\tre-run the candidate threads noted in the build notes and add them.\n    29\t\n    30\tLookup is by exact key membership in ``keys`` -- no fuzzy matching, no family\n    31\tfallback (unlike :mod:`mes.code_feel`): a code with no entry simply returns\n    32\tan empty list, which is the honest answer when nothing verified.\n    33\t\"\"\"\n    34\t\n    35\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    36\t\n    37\timport re\n    38\tfrom typing import Any\n    39\t\n    40\t_CODE_RE = re.compile(r\"^[PBCU][0-9A-F]{4}$\", re.IGNORECASE)\n    41\t\n    42\t#: Non-code keys this table recognises. A code (matches _CODE_RE) is always\n    43\t#: a valid key regardless of whether anything is tabulated for it yet.\n    44\tFAMILIES = {\"EVAP\", \"network_cascade\", \"misfire\"}\n    45\tJOBS = {\n    46\t    \"esim\", \"purge_valve\", \"canister\",\n    47\t    \"oil_change\", \"spark_plugs\", \"engine_air_filter\", \"cabin_air_filter\",\n    48\t    \"brake_fluid\", \"transfer_case\", \"drive_belt\", \"battery_12v\",\n    49\t    \"window_riser\", \"tpms\", \"zf8hp_fluid\",\n    50\t}\n    51\tKNOWN_NON_CODE_KEYS = FAMILIES | JOBS\n    52\t\n    53\tVERIFIED_AT = \"2026-10-07\"\n    54\t\n    55\tLINKS: tuple[dict[str, Any], ...] = (\n    56\t    # --- EVAP family: P0440/P0441/P0455/P0456/P0457, ESIM, purge valve, canister ---\n    57\t    {\n    58\t        \"id\": \"yt-evap-p0440-fixed\",\n    59\t        \"keys\": [\"P0440\", \"P0441\", \"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"EVAP\"],\n    60\t        \"title\": \"P0440 EVAP Fault on Alfa Romeo Giulia & Stelvio 2.0 — FIXED!\",\n    61\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G9M--Poudm8\",\n    62\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n    63\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n    64\t        \"covers\": \"Hands-on diagnosis and fix of an EVAP fault on a Giulia/Stelvio 2.0, \"\n    65\t                  \"walking the actual leak path on the car.\",\n    66\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"giulia_2.0t\",\n    67\t        \"date\": None,\n    68\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n    69\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n    70\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n    71\t    },\n    72\t    {\n    73\t        \"id\": \"yt-evap-canister-giulia\",\n    74\t        \"keys\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"EVAP\", \"canister\"],\n    75\t        \"title\": \"Evap Canister Replacement Alfa Romeo Giulia\",\n    76\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UJh89VxrVIA\",\n    77\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n    78\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n    79\t        \"covers\": \"Full R&R of the EVAP canister on a Giulia, the same canister fitted to \"\n    80\t                  \"the Stelvio 2.0T.\",\n    81\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"giulia_2.0t\",\n    82\t        \"date\": None,\n    83\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n    84\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n    85\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n    86\t    },\n    87\t    {\n    88\t        \"id\": \"yt-evap-esim-tips\",\n    89\t        \"keys\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"EVAP\", \"esim\", \"canister\"],\n    90\t        \"title\": \"Evaporative System Integrity Module (ESIM) Replacement Tips\",\n    91\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=40h9LbzwVxQ\",\n    92\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n    93\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n    94\t        \"covers\": \"ESIM replacement/diagnosis tips from a parts-channel tech, relevant \"\n    95\t                  \"wherever the ESIM is the suspect part rather than the canister body.\",\n    96\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"generic_obd\",\n    97\t        \"date\": None,\n    98\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n    99\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n   100\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n   101\t    },\n   102\t    {\n   103\t        \"id\": \"yt-evap-purge-valve-fiat-alfa\",\n   104\t        \"keys\": [\"P0440\", \"P0441\", \"EVAP\", \"purge_valve\"],\n   105\t        \"title\": \"PURGE CONTROL VALVE LOCATION REPLACEMENT EXPLAINED FIAT, ALFA ROMEO\",\n   106\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YfXQWoCncA4\",\n   107\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n   108\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n   109\t        \"covers\": \"Purge control valve location and replacement across the shared \"\n   110\t                  \"Fiat/Alfa Romeo platform parts bin.\",\n   111\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"generic_obd\",\n   112\t        \"date\": None,\n   113\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n   114\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n   115\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n   116\t    },\n   117\t\n   118\t    # --- misfire: P0300-P0304 ---------------------------------------------\n   119\t    {\n   120\t        \"id\": \"yt-misfire-p0300-coil\",\n   121\t        \"keys\": [\"P0300\", \"P0301\", \"P0302\", \"P0303\", \"P0304\", \"misfire\"],\n   122\t        \"title\": \"How To Fix An Engine Misfire-P0300 (Bad Ignition Coil)\",\n   123\t        \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6icmfICvyp0\",\n   124\t        \"source\": \"youtube\",\n   125\t        \"kind\": \"how_to_video\",\n   126\t        \"covers\": \"Generic coil-pack misfire diagnosis walkthrough -- not Alfa-specific, \"\n   127\t                  \"no platform-specific misfire video verified; included as the general \"\n   128\t                  \"diagnostic method (swap-the-coil test) that does apply to the 2.0T.\",\n   129\t        \"vehicle_fit\": \"generic_obd\",\n   130\t        \"date\": None,\n   131\t        \"reputation\": \"medium\",\n   132\t        \"verified_at\": VERIFIED_AT,\n   133\t        \"verified_how\": \"youtube_oembed\",\n   134\t    },\n   135\t\n   136\t    # --- oil_change ---------------------------------------------------------\n   137\t    {\n   138\t        \"id\": \"yt-oil-change-giulia-stelvio\",\n   139\t        \"keys\": [\"oil_change\"],\n   140\t        \"title\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0