{"parentUuid":"d03a4044-f9e7-4ed6-a4dc-50bbe6e07f5d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3bf9b52fb2ec01e6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfovREB9pEC4aKkZqLjUp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XnQBmZq3uGAq13aFrUqxiJ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\experience.py","old_string":"Every entry was checked on 2026-10-07 (``verified_at``) either by an HTTP GET\nreturning 200 with a browser User-Agent (``verified_how: \"http_200\"``) or via\nthe YouTube oEmbed endpoint returning 200 with a title (``verified_how:\n\"youtube_oembed\"``, and that returned title is stored verbatim). Nothing\nbelow was invented and nothing that failed verification was kept.\n\nKNOWN LIMITATION -- forum threads: stelvioforum.com, giuliaforums.com,\nalfabb.com and alfaowner.com (all XenForo, apparently sharing one vendor) sit\nbehind a JavaScript proof-of-work bot challenge that returns HTTP 202 with a\nchallenge page to any plain HTTP client, never the real thread -- confirmed\nagainst a dozen thread URLs across all four domains during this build. A\nplain ``urllib``/``requests`` GET cannot pass that challenge (it requires\nexecuting the page's JS), so no thread on those four domains could be\nverified as HTTP 200 and none is included here, even though the threads\nthemselves clearly exist and are on-topic. The practical effect: this table\nis YouTube-heavy and forum-light. If a future verification pass gains a way\nto pass that challenge (a real browser session, a cookie jar primed by one),\nre-run the candidate threads noted in the build notes and add them.","new_string":"Every entry was checked on 2026-10-07 (``verified_at``) by one of:\n- an HTTP GET returning 200 with a browser User-Agent (``verified_how:\n  \"http_200\"``);\n- the YouTube oEmbed endpoint returning 200 with a title (``verified_how:\n  \"youtube_oembed\"``, and that returned title is stored verbatim);\n- a real headless-browser navigation over the Chrome DevTools Protocol,\n  reading ``document.title`` and the first post's text off the rendered page\n  (``verified_how: \"browser_cdp\"``). Nothing below was invented and nothing\n  that failed verification was kept.\n\nFORUM THREADS -- stelvioforum.com, giuliaforums.com, alfabb.com and\nalfaowner.com (all XenForo, apparently sharing one vendor) sit behind a\nJavaScript proof-of-work bot challenge that returns HTTP 202 with a\nchallenge page to any plain HTTP client, never the real thread -- confirmed\nagainst a dozen thread URLs across all four domains during the original\nbuild. A plain ``urllib``/``requests`` GET cannot pass that challenge (it\nrequires executing the page's JS), so no thread on those four domains could\nbe verified as HTTP 200 that way. A later pass (2026-10-07) drove headless\nEdge over CDP instead -- a real browser session executes the challenge JS\nlike any visitor -- and that got through cleanly for every candidate thread\ntried, so forum_thread entries verified ``browser_cdp`` are now included\nbelow. Any thread that still returns a bot-wall title (\"Just a moment\",\n\"Attention Required\", etc.) or has no readable post text under that method\nis left out, same as before."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":96289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":975,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XnQBmZq3uGAq13aFrUqxiJ":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\experience.py","old_string":"Every entry was checked on 2026-10-07 (``verified_at``) either by an HTTP GET\nreturning 200 with a browser User-Agent (``verified_how: \"http_200\"``) or via\nthe YouTube oEmbed endpoint returning 200 with a title (``verified_how:\n\"youtube_oembed\"``, and that returned title is stored verbatim). Nothing\nbelow was invented and nothing that failed verification was kept.\n\nKNOWN LIMITATION -- forum threads: stelvioforum.com, giuliaforums.com,\nalfabb.com and alfaowner.com (all XenForo, apparently sharing one vendor) sit\nbehind a JavaScript proof-of-work bot challenge that returns HTTP 202 with a\nchallenge page to any plain HTTP client, never the real thread -- confirmed\nagainst a dozen thread URLs across all four domains during this build. A\nplain ``urllib``/``requests`` GET cannot pass that challenge (it requires\nexecuting the page's JS), so no thread on those four domains could be\nverified as HTTP 200 and none is included here, even though the threads\nthemselves clearly exist and are on-topic. The practical effect: this table\nis YouTube-heavy and forum-light. If a future verification pass gains a way\nto pass that challenge (a real browser session, a cookie jar primed by one),\nre-run the candidate threads noted in the build notes and add them.","new_string":"Every entry was checked on 2026-10-07 (``verified_at``) by one of:\n- an HTTP GET returning 200 with a browser User-Agent (``verified_how:\n  \"http_200\"``);\n- the YouTube oEmbed endpoint returning 200 with a title (``verified_how:\n  \"youtube_oembed\"``, and that returned title is stored verbatim);\n- a real headless-browser navigation over the Chrome DevTools Protocol,\n  reading ``document.title`` and the first post's text off the rendered page\n  (``verified_how: \"browser_cdp\"``). Nothing below was invented and nothing\n  that failed verification was kept.\n\nFORUM THREADS -- stelvioforum.com, giuliaforums.com, alfabb.com and\nalfaowner.com (all XenForo, apparently sharing one vendor) sit behind a\nJavaScript proof-of-work bot challenge that returns HTTP 202 with a\nchallenge page to any plain HTTP client, never the real thread -- confirmed\nagainst a dozen thread URLs across all four domains during the original\nbuild. A plain ``urllib``/``requests`` GET cannot pass that challenge (it\nrequires executing the page's JS), so no thread on those four domains could\nbe verified as HTTP 200 that way. A later pass (2026-10-07) drove headless\nEdge over CDP instead -- a real browser session executes the challenge JS\nlike any visitor -- and that got through cleanly for every candidate thread\ntried, so forum_thread entries verified ``browser_cdp`` are now included\nbelow. Any thread that still returns a bot-wall title (\"Just a moment\",\n\"Attention Required\", etc.) or has no readable post text under that method\nis left out, same as before."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bee4a1ba-4109-4d3e-8ca3-2a693d5d2187","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfovRDwzy6tmdumEeHBP2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"797172da-9e8c-4ea6-9a38-375c4263b44f","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:44:13.974Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
